| tips =
*{{A|Sow}} and {{A|Reap}}'s 25% current Health {{D|True}} damage can be used in conjunction with another damage multiplier, like {{A|Roar}} or {{D|Viral}} statuses (along with Reap's '''Damage Vulnerability''') to achieve a 100% Health {{D|True}} damage drain.
** When using {{A|Roar}}, 255% {{Stat|Ability Strength}} is required, this will amplify Roar's buff to 76.5% and Reap's damage vulnerability to 127.5%, increasing the 25% HP True damage up to 100%. 
*** Although {{M|Precision Intensify}} can be used to amplify {{A|Roar}}'s buff if subsumed over the {{A|Exalted Shadow}}, it can damper other abilities in the kit like {{A|Reap}} and {{A|Gloom}} slow, while also having worse scaling compared to slotting other mods instead like {{M|Umbral Intensify}} or {{M|Transient Fortitude}}.
** When using {{D|Viral}} statuses, the amount of {{Stat|Ability Strength}} required to amplify Reap's [[Damage Vulnerability]] to achieve 100% Health {{D|True}} damage varies.
*** With '''1''' status, only 200% Strength is needed.
*** With '''2''' statuses, only 156% Strength is needed.
*** With '''3''' statuses, only 120% Strength is needed, etc.
*** With '''9''' statuses or more, no amount of strength is needed since the 25% {{D|True}} damage will be instantly increased to '''100%'''.
** Alternatively, {{Resource|Emerald Archon Shard}}s can be combined with {{A|Tempest Barrage}} (and {{M|Viral Tempest}}) as another damage multiplier to further reduce the amount of {{Stat|Ability Strength}} required.
*** With 1 {{Resource|Tauforged Emerald Archon Shard}}, only 148% Strength is needed.
*** With 2 {{Resource|Tauforged Emerald Archon Shard}}, only 108% Strength is needed.
*** While 3 or more {{Resource|Emerald Archon Shard}} can keep reducing the Strength needed, it would remove the guarantee of {{M|Viral Tempest}} applying {{D|Viral}} statuses.
** While this strategy is popularly claimed to be a one-shot, it is technically a '''two-shot''' due to the [[Damage Vulnerability]] from Reap applied '''after''' the {{D|True}} damage is dealt, hence the usage of {{M|Shadow Haze}} may be advised to save the need for a second Reap cast, due to an enemy often dying from the initial explosion's {{D|Blast}} damage.
**  A {{Companion|Shade}} or {{Companion|Huras Kubrow}} is recommended to keep stealth while casting abilities.
